 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Sure thing. In one scene, music is used to build tension, while in another it sets the mood of a dark night. Which one do you want to focus on? That's called silence. You could compare a scene where every piece of music is crucial to the story to one where the music is barely there. How about the power of a theme song? Exactly. That theme song can go from cheerful to terrifying in a split second. No problem. Just remember, the most powerful scenes often mix it up, using a mix of quiet and loud for maximum impact.",
